# Lock Locators / Element-Finding Pipeline

## Architecture

The Lock Locators feature saves the CSS/text selector that was used to find an element during a successful test run. On re-runs, these "locked" selectors are tried first (150ms fast path) for instant element finding.

## Full Data Flow

### 1. Test Execution (Desktop app)

- `playwright-recorder.js` `executeAction()` (line ~7907) calls `ActionHandlers.executeAction(this, action, { timeout })`
- ActionHandlers delegates to handler functions: `handleClick`, `handleFill`, `handleHover`, etc.
- Each handler calls `ctx.findElementWithRetry(action)` which sets `ctx._lastWorkingSelector`
- `enrichResult(ctx, result, action)` wraps every handler return to attach `workingSelector`

### 2. Element Finding (`findElementWithRetry` in `playwright-recorder.js` line ~7639)

- **Layer 1**: Try LOCKED selector (`optimizedSelector` from `selectorObj`) — 150ms timeout
- **Layer 2**: `SmartFinder.find(recipe)` — sets `lastSuccessfulSelector` via `_recordLearningAndReturn`
- **Layer 3**: Legacy `_findElement` fallback
- Each layer sets `this._lastWorkingSelector` on success

### 3. Selector Generation (when SmartFinder finds element but no CSS string)

- `_buildSelectorFromRecipe()` — constructs from recipe data (testId, ariaLabel, role+text, text, id, name)
- `_extractSelectorFromLocator()` — queries actual DOM element attributes
- `enrichResult()` — fallback from `action.selectorObj` fields
- **LAST RESORT**: `getActionLabel(action)` → `text="label"` selector

### 4. IPC to Frontend

- `recorder.emit('test-step-complete', { stepIndex, workingSelector, strategyType, healed, newSelector })`
- `recorder.emit('test-complete', { stepResults })` — includes `workingSelector` per step
- `index.js` forwards via `sendToWebapp('playwright-test-complete', ...)`

### 5. Frontend Lock (`PlaywrightRecorderPage.tsx` `handleLockLocators` line ~3862)

- Iterates `actions[]`, matches with `testExecutionResult.stepResults` by index
- Writes `action.selectorObj.optimizedSelector = workingSelector`
- Persists to localStorage (`test_cases`, `flowstral_test_cases`, `unified_test_case_{id}`)

